    passage: "Good morning. I'm here to present findings from the after action review of last month's operation. Overall, mission objectives were achieved. However, several areas require attention. First, coordination between ground and air elements experienced delays averaging forty minutes, primarily due to communication challenges. While our equipment functioned properly, procedural differences between services created confusion during time-critical phases. Second, logistical planning underestimated fuel consumption by approximately eighteen percent. This forced mid-operation adjustments that, while successful, reduced operational tempo. Third, intelligence support was generally adequate, but there were gaps in our understanding of civilian movement patterns, which complicated our efforts to minimize disruption to local populations. On the positive side, the multinational composition of the force proved highly effective, and liaison arrangements worked well. The key lesson is that technical interoperability is necessary but insufficient. We need better harmonization of procedures and more realistic planning assumptions. Full report with recommendations will be distributed by Friday.",
